ather, excellent computer skills. Weakness: relatively weak memory for numbers, regarded as pretentious. So strengths: reliability, stress resilience, technical (weather, computer). Concerns: memory for numbers (attention/accuracy), pretentious (crew cooperation).\n\nC: can make correct decisions quickly, difficulty communicating ideas, regarded as egocentric, not willing to further education, keeps calm in crisis, puts concern for others above everything. Strengths: decision quality, stress resilience, crew cooperation (concern for others). Concerns: communication difficulty, egocentric, not willing to further education (adaptability).\n\nD: responds to unexpected events adequately, can concentrate very well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously, regarded as know-it-all, considered moody. Strengths: adaptability, attention, problem solving, responsibility. Concerns: know-it-all (crew cooperation), moody (stress resilience maybe).\n\nWe need to pick best overall fit. Likely Candidate C has good decision making, calm, concern for others, but communication difficulty and egocentric may be big issues. Candidate B has strong reliability and stress, but pretentious and weak memory for numbers could be safety risk. Candidate D has strong problem solving, responsibility, concentration, but moody and know-it-all may affect crew. Candidate A has technical competence but unfriendly and show-off.\n\nWhich is best? Probably Candidate B seems balanced: conscientious, handles stress, good weather assessment, computer skills, but memory for numbers weak could be issue for navigation. However, reliability and stress are critical. Pretentious may affect crew but maybe manageable.\n\nCandidate D has strong problem solving and responsibility, but moody could affect calmness under pressure. Also know-it-all may affect crew.\n\nCandidate C's communication difficulty is serious for cockpit communication.\n\nThus maybe Candidate B is best overall.\n\nWe need to state recommendation for Candidate B, referencing facts: very conscientious (reliability), handles stress well (stress resilience), good at assessing weather (technical competence), but note concerns: weak memory for numbers (attention) and pretentious (crew cooperation). Explain why strengths outweigh concerns.\n\nLet's produce public message."}
